  - "Follows the work of Smith et al. (2020)" → 20% citation  
  - "Aligns with the framework proposed by Lee (2022)" → 20% citation  
  - The rest describes *how* the model is adapted to existing frameworks (e.g., "binary classification for demographic fairness"), which is derivative of prior literature.  
  The citation content is substantial but not the core innovation.

**Key Insight**: This paragraph has **moderate technical contribution** (30%) because it builds on prior work but adds **practical, implementable solutions** (binary labels and post-processing). The rest is contextualization of existing research.

---

